 155:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****     [..]
 156:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****     By default, after the @ref HAL_USART_Init() and when the state is HAL_USART_STATE_RESET
 157:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****     all callbacks are set to the corresponding weak (surcharged) functions:
 158:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****     examples @ref HAL_USART_TxCpltCallback(), @ref HAL_USART_RxHalfCpltCallback().
 159:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****     Exception done for MspInit and MspDeInit functions that are respectively
 160:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****     reset to the legacy weak (surcharged) functions in the @ref HAL_USART_Init()
 161:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****     and @ref HAL_USART_DeInit() only when these callbacks are null (not registered beforehand).
 162:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****     If not, MspInit or MspDeInit are not null, the @ref HAL_USART_Init() and @ref HAL_USART_DeInit(
 163:Drivers/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_usart.c ****     keep and use the user MspInit/MspDeInit callbacks (registered beforehand).
